WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.370
In the Friendship Cup's third match,

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:07.020
Yuzu fought Mr. Tokumatsu.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.200
During her duel, she used words 
that stimulated my heart.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.030
The fun is only getting started!

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.160
Battle.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.530
Mozarta attacks Lightshower.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.350
Go! Get fired up! Let your blood boil!

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.410
Well? Gives you the shivers, doesn't it?

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.940
I'm sure she meant them as a message to me.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.910
Yuya, you're watching, right?

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.120
You aren't alone.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.530
It's finished!

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.130
The powerful duel that had us in a 
cold sweat is finally over!

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.130
The winner is Yuzu!

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.760
Yuya... I did it.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.920
I gave it my all.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.580
D-Wheels.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.780
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.430
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:13.880
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.060
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:54.320
Futile Screams

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:01.460
Yuzu thought I was depressed 
from losing to Jack.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.940
And she wasn't the only one. 
Mr. Tokumatsu, too...

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.940
He knew that if he lost, he'd be 
sent to the forced-labor facility.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:10.860
Still, he called out to me.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.000
Yuzu, Mr. Tokumatsu... Thank you.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.880
Your feelings reached me!

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.600
Yuzu and Enjoy Chojiro's magnificent duel

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.120
has united the 200,000 spectators!

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.240
This truly is the Friendship Cup!

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.820
If you try, you guys really can do it.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:35.290
Now, let's keep it up and move to the next match!

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.760
Okay, bring it on!

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.230
I have to be the one to go after Yuzu!

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.870
The last match of the Friendship Cup's first day is

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.940
Serena versus Tony!

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:45.900
Serena!

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.870
Serena?

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:50.400
The next female duelist after Yuzu, Serena,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.440
and a rising Commons star, Tony Simmons.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.350
I can't wait to see what cards they use!

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.880
Again, not me?

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.650
I don't get to play today, eh?

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.240
I could've just spent the day 
sleeping in this fluffy bed.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.360
I got my hopes up for nothing.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.870
Okay! Counting on you, Tony!

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.830
This time, spur the Commons to action!

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:20.510
Disappointed that you aren't 
the one to fight the girl?

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.240
That will still happen.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:27.710
If she's the duelist I think she is,

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.240
she should have no problem advancing.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.510
Most likely, she will reach the finals.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.420
She'll be quite popular, too.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.660
Then you will crush her...

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.890
And Jack Atlas, afterward!

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:47.080
You must defeat those two, who possess 
both popularity and talent,

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.500
and deliver a shock to City.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.600
That is what you're here for.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.250
I'm counting on you, Sergey.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.700
If Serena loses, she'll be sent underground, too...

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.010
I can't let that happen! I won't accept it!

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:04.250
It's the Friendship Cup. But lose, 
and you're sent underground.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.720
Letting it happen, even knowing that...

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:10.690
Give me a break, Administrative Council! 
You can hear me, right?

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:13.340
Stop this tournament right now!

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.390
Don't make a show out of us!

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:19.060
Tony and Serena's fierce battle has 
the whole stadium on its feet!

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:23.600
It's a truly passionate duel, befitting the 
day's final match.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.290
Go, Tony!

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.920
Fight, Serena!

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.370
Currently, Tony has 3000 life.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.160
Serena has 2500.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.310
Can she turn it around this turn?

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.060
My turn!

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:39.100
I summon Lunalight Purple Butterfly!

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:45.690
And I activate my spell card 
Polymerization from my hand!

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.590
I fuse Lunalight Cat Dancer and 
Lunalight Purple Butterfly.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:55.030
The beautiful beast that dances in the moonlight!

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:56.920
The butterfly with purple poison!

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:01.670
Swirl in the moon's gravity and 
be reborn with new power!

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.380
Fusion Summon!

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:11.060
Appear, graceful beast who 
dances in moonlit fields!

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.710
Lunalight Panther Dancer!

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.460
Here it is!

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.890
Serena Fusion Summons again!

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:26.200
Do all female duelists of the new generation 
use Fusion, do you think?

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.380
Now that I mention it, they look the same, right?

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:31.900
Are they sisters or something?

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.640
Sisters, eh? I see.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.060
I activate my trap Bottomless Trap Hole!

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:43.350
When you summon a monster with 
1500 or more attack points,

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:46.250
I destroy that monster and banish it!

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.180
That won't work.

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:53.390
Lunalight Panther Dance cannot 
be destroyed by card effects!

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.230
What?

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:59.200
Lunalight Panther Dancer can attack 
each of your monsters twice!

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:00.930
Each of them twice?

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.170
Battle!

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:05.870
Panther Dancer attacks Archfiend Zombie-Skull!

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.810
I took damage, but I guess you can't 
destroy it... Which means I win!

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:17.560
The effect of my Equip Spell 
Zombie Heart activates!

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:21.720
At the end of a turn in which battle 
occurred with a monster

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.520
possessing more attack points than mine,

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:29.480
I can deal that monster's attack points, 
2500 in other words, as damage to you.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.050
You have exactly 2500 life remaining.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.720
I bet you regret that you couldn't 
finish me off with that attack.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.330
It's true, I couldn't destroy it with the first attack.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.960
The first one, that is.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:42.810
What?

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.780
Go, Panther Dancer!

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:47.350
Your second attack against Zombie-Skull!

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:58.060
The second time, I destroy it!

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:03.080
And during the Battle Phase, Panther Dancer's 
attack points increase by 200!

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:08.410
Which means it'll deal 3000 points 
twice to my second monster.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:11.270
And the 3200 twice to my third...

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:12.670
That's right.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:16.400
By the time the fourth attack is 
finished, your life will be gone.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.510
Seems you'll be the one filled with regret.

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:19.820
Tony...

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:23.480
The second monster is also destroyed 
on the second attack.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:27.640
The last is finished on the second attack, as well!

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:32.590
My brother... picked Tsukikage over me...

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.600
The winner is Serena!

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:38.060
After Yuzu Hiiragi, that's two 
female winners in a row.

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:40.590
You see that, boys?

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.030
This is the age of the female duelist!

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.700
Male or female is irrelevant.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:50.060
What matters is the training the duelist receives.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.240
Clearly, she has received excellent training.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:56.440
She didn't disappoint our expectations 
at all, did she?

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.790
Serena...

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:05.080
That concludes all the matches on 
the Friendship Cup's first day.

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:12.460
Everyone! Did you enjoy yourselves?

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.780
Yeah, yeah... Sounding good!

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:20.760
Now, let's close with the slogan once more!

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.970
City is united as one!

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:25.310
Huh?

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:30.170
The exit is this way! No pushing, no pushing!

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:33.480
Hey... "We're all friends," right?

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:36.450
Finish it off properly, won't you?

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.700
"We're all friends," my eye!

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:46.140
How can you have a Friendship Cup, in which 
the losers are sent underground?

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:49.540
Serena won, but Tony lost...

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.210
Which means he'll be sent down there.

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:54.720
Th-This is wrong!

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.350
I won't acknowledge it! I won't!

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:58.680
A tournament like this!

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:03.640
But what can I do now?

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:07.480
Standing here and screaming won't prompt 
the Administrative Council to act.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:10.430
One win, two losses on the first day.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:13.590
At least you managed to save 
a bit of face at the end.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:18.060
Yuzu Hiiragi won, as well. Is she 
a member of the Lancers?

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:22.840
It's true that she is a duelist from 
our Standard Dimension.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:26.540
In terms of ability, too, she is 
as capable as the Lancers.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:30.320
So including her, it's two wins and two losses.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:35.610
If you're here to protect our dimension, that does 
not inspire tremendous confidence.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.280
That's my opinion, anyway. Chairman?

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:39.700
Indeed.

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:43.020
But let's see what happens tomorrow.

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:46.680
Forgive me. We shall be going, then.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.730
Wait a minute.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:55.160
Now that the day's matches are finished,

00:10:55.160 --> 00:11:00.240
why not stay and enjoy a meal 
with us, to share our thoughts?

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:03.800
We've invited a special guest, as well.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.280
Who is it?

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.480
The leading duelist, known throughout the world.

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:12.350
The one against whom the Lancers 
were completely helpless.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.360
The pride of City.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:15.950
The King of Duelists.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:17.690
Yes, it is he.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:30.640
J-Jack... Atlas...

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.240
Why didn't they call on me?

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:45.130
I, Shingo Sawatari, ace of LDS 
and the Lancers' top duelist...

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:48.020
The tournament's first day is so important!

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:51.240
How can you do something so foolish?!

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.970
No, you can't do it... That much is obvious.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:58.570
I'll ask my daddy to have everyone associated 
with this tournament fired!

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.810
I'll have you fired, you hear me?

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:16.300
Well, for today, I'll accept this 
feast as a suitable apology.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:24.890
But tomorrow, you'd better put me in... 
I want to show everyone how I win.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.010
This is delicious!

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:31.780
I've never had such delicious meat before.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:39.960
I'm so glad I entered the Friendship Cup.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:42.470
I bet Yuzu's grateful to me, too.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:52.050
But didn't she join the tournament to warn 
people about the interdimensional war?

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:55.200
But during the duel, she didn't 
say a word about it.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.990
Just "Let your blood boil!"

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:59.450
And "It gives me shivers!"

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:04.360
Oh, well. Tomorrow, I'll come 
out firing on all cylinders.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.880
Delicious!

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:14.660
I gave absolutely everything I had in that duel.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:23.450
But I'm not sure if I actually reached 
Yuya or cheered him up.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:29.790
I wish I could see him and talk to him, face to face.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.310
I don't know what I can do right now.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:41.070
But I can't just sit here, depressed.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:50.010
For Yuzu and Mr. Tokumatsu, who encouraged 
me, I have to do something.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:53.580
Your way of dueling is mere self-satisfaction.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.310
It is a far cry from entertainment!

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:01.440
Is it possible... Is this what 
Jack wanted to tell me?

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.520
To duel not for yourself, but for someone else?

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:05.460
No!

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:10.260
There was no such kindness 
in the way he dueled.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:16.280
I don't see how that can be true entertainment.

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:25.060
To me, entertainment is the way Dad dueled.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:30.550
To bring a smile to the faces of the watching 
crowd and the duelist you're fighting...

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.460
That's true entertainment.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:34.920
Right, Dad?

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:43.630
You say Yuzu Hiiragi was the best 
of the first day's duelists, King?

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:45.440
She had talent, of course.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:48.910
But it's more in the way she seemed 
to fight to convey something.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:52.000
Indeed, she did seem to 
be making some appeal.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:56.320
Enjoy Chojiro was an excellent match for her.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:15:00.070
Their duel had great impact. I'm glad I saw it.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:04.020
Chairman, you like him, don't you?

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:05.720
It's a shame he lost.

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:08.410
And now, we'll never again...

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:11.960
Excuse me.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:15.100
That boy was also on the list, wasn't he?

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:20.160
Forgive me. Conditions demanded 
a change in the lineup.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:23.390
That Tsukikage ninja, right?

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:26.870
You seemed to have some scheme in mind.

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:37.240
Tsu... Tsukikage...

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:41.490
I wish I could have seen the boy duel.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.960
Seen Layra duel? Why?

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:48.710
He has the same eyes I once had.

00:15:56.520 --> 00:16:00.190
Back then, I was always afraid of something.

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:02.410
I lived life constantly on edge.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.380
Yes, until I was just about his age.

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:09.500
I see. Forgive me for saying this, King,

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:11.850
but I heard you were born among the Commons.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.890
There is nothing to forgive.

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:18.410
I was born a Commons. And due to 
that life, at the bottom of the barrel,

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:23.190
I decided to crawl out, to find my way to the top.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:26.560
The Commons are my pride and my origin.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:30.770
Did that boy grow up in an 
environment similar to mine?

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:32.780
Impressive, King...

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:36.120
I compliment your keen powers of observation.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:37.640
Oh, really?

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.930
Isn't that boy your little brother?

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:44.920
If it's no imposition,

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:49.830
I would like to ask the king what it was that 
made him choose the duelist's path.

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.100
It could be useful for Layra to hear.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.460
It was a card that started it all.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.830
That card fell to me, from the 
world of the Tops above.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.340
Someone had, perhaps, lost it.

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:42.730
Or maybe they didn't want it anymore, 
and just threw it away.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.040
More likely the latter.

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:49.360
The card itself was not especially valuable.

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:50.750
But the moment I saw it,

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:54.220
it was as if I'd had a divine revelation.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:07.020
And that's when I thought...

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:12.730
I needed to return that card 
to the world up there.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:15.140
With my own hands.

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:18.060
To do that, I had to become strong.

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:23.240
As a person... As a duelist... I had 
to become stronger than anyone.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.570
I've heard you come from a foreign country.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:31.870
I'm not sure why you had your team 
take part in the Friendship Cup,

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:35.730
but if you're trying to accomplish something...

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:36.690
Do not falter!

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:41.040
Your name is Layra, yes?

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.990
I hope that you set your mind to something.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:46.700
So that, someday, I can see you gallantly duel.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:51.340
I'm honored.

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:56.970
I'm sure Layra is proud to have the King of 
Duelists, Jack Atlas, tell him such a thing.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:06.140
U-Um, I've brought you a letter.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:14.300
Th-This is from the director?

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:18.000
"It has been some time, Number 227.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:21.740
Or perhaps I shall call you by 
your Duel Chasers title,

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:24.230
which you may retain for tomorrow alone.

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:27.780
Duel Chaser 227.

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:31.210
According to tomorrow's tournament bracket,

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:35.220
you're set to fight Yuya Sakaki in the first round.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:39.420
A shame it isn't Hugo, the one 
who humiliated you like that...

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:42.890
But I wish to see you bury Yuya Sakaki.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:47.400
Once you beat him, I shall 
restore your former job."

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:49.770
D-Director, you...

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:53.400
You haven't abandoned me, after all!

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:58.750
Ever since I lost the duel to that man, Hugo,

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:02.170
I... I've been cast down to a Commons

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:05.780
and pursued as a criminal 
by my former comrades.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:10.320
Just when I was arrested and thought 
I'd be thrown in prison,

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:13.390
I was brought to this penthouse instead!

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:15.780
At last, I understand why!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:26.950
Watch me, director.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:30.370
This time, I will meet your expectations.

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:32.460
Along with this card!

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:52.160
The way I want to duel is with my 
father's entertainment duel.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.520
I reject Jack's way of dueling.

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:56.580
I reject the Friendship Cup, too.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:01.960
A tournament where you kick people down and 
sadden them to elevate yourself is wrong.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:05.530
I'll just have to make everyone see that!

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:52.420
Everyone, do you know what happens 
to the people who lose duels here?

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:56.500
They're sent as forced labor to an underground 
waste-processing facility!

00:23:57.990 --> 00:24:01.350
What's wrong with that? It's only natural.

00:24:01.810 --> 00:24:04.590
Only natural? That's wrong!

00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:07.910
Yuya, the most important thing is winning.

00:24:09.230 --> 00:24:12.760
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Silver Sword.

00:24:13.480 --> 00:24:15.510
The fun is only getting started!
